    <h2>฿ 8 — Mr. the Painter and the Coyote's Breakfast</h2>

    <p class="date">November 14, 2026</p>

    <p>
        Rome is my mind. But in my head is a new volunteer at hostel. Mercy told me that, he arrives every years at the same time. 
        He’s house painter. At hostel he spends few weeks doing minor repairs. He also makes some extra money by painting fancy residestio   n 
       of people, who are enough reach to live middle on nowhere by choice. Before met him, I was imaging him like snufkin, who as well, 
       had been visited Moominvalley once a year. He appeared close to this picture, but because of his roots, more like a child 
      of Pocahontas and a lovely boy in a hat. I was out friendly – he won’t steal my job – seems to be of similar age to me – 
     and last but not least, his looks perfectly matching with our weirdo small world. But! At the beginning he took to me with a pinch 
     of salt – playing the role of mincing decadent. <br></br>
    <b>mister coyote – mister ice breaker</b>. In the morning Pan the Pintor used to sit on the stairs leading to Mercy chamber. 
   He had been drinking coffee, rolling cigarettes and of course watching coyotes with turtle–coyote. Everytime when I was passing them, 
   I was saying welcoming “hola”, but he only nodded nonchalantly with his dirty baseball cap. I was sure, he  stained it on purpose, 
   such a poser! Maybe I was overreacting a bit, yet his ignorance for me was just painful. Happily, at least coyote likes me, and even more 
   he likes eat greens… Perhaps his soul is already belongs to coyote, but his culinary tastes is still turtle thing. This day, 
   because of waking up too late, I couldn’t go for breakfast to the my lil bakery. So I was rapidly preparing my supper as the first meal 
   of the day. When the coyote, by some mirecoules, smelled the scentless smell of lamb's lettuce he hit the ground running to the kitchen for workers. Pan the Pintor, shocked by the uprising of reptile followed him.<br></br>
    In that way our friendship begun – from coyote eating my morning vitamins and my native language, which triumphally went ahead be 
   fore thoughts – “Oh yes coyotie, of course, with princess of cleanliness is better, than with some mister roll” – because, his name 
    – Pan the Pintor – in spanish – is like <i>Roll the Pintor</i>. Very funny, at least for me…. tbc…

